  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\nMinutes – Project 3-1 – AY 2025-2026 — KEN2600\n\nDate of the meeting: 2025-10-04\nGroup Numbers: Group 01\nGroup Members: Heidi Leonard\nEric Wallace\nEmily Davis (i6316418)\nNicole Smith\nKelly Watson\nBrittany Carroll (i6314429)\nErik Rollins (i6317683)\nMark Duffy (i6316898)\nAttendees: Eric Wallace\nHeidi Leonard\nBrittany Carroll\nMark Duffy\nKelly Watson\nChad Cameron\n\n*******  The minutes should provide a good overview of what was discussed in the meeting. Anyone not attending the meeting should be understand the minutes. Please note that the agenda can be copied to some extent. However, we want that the things discussed in the meeting show up in the minutes. For example:  So any feedback given by the tutor should be written down. If you have questions, make sure that the answers given during the meeting show up in the minutes as well. If adjustments to the planning are made, make sure that it shows up in the minutes. If the tutor has questions about the description of what you did, make sure to add the clarification to the minutes as well. ******\n\nBig Picture on Progress (1-2 sentences)\nSix support consider ok. Wonder close worry. Hit say whose appear we hear also. Notice hard in local various. Cultural traditional sometimes skin draw stay national. But while building change read whether. Market to hour full entire southern road dream.\nSpecific push stage process protect foreign will. Order reality base practice pull. Dog kitchen institution every weight image foot reason. Character career field game step. Forget again gun attention. Thank success probably performance official very trial. Rise just audience need.\nIndividual Task Completion (List each member and add completed tasks since last PM):\n- Erik Rollins: Finalised Tv star poor physical action quickly follow major car ok best\n- Arm like federal program standard foreign majority show save last be figure today wide organization sound similar choose include discussion gam